From b5c185bbc559e7035eed7d49e77f2c3321b60d9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:17:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] media: apple: vxd: add the V4L2 stateless H.264 m2m
 device

R3/R4 scaffolding on the rkvdec stateless template: /dev/video node
with media controller entity, mplane m2m queues, the request API
mandatory on the output queue, and the full V4L2_CID_STATELESS_H264_*
control set (SPS/PPS/DECODE_PARAMS/SCALING_MATRIX/PRED_WEIGHTS/
SLICE_PARAMS dynamic array/DECODE_MODE/START_CODE/PROFILE/LEVEL).
Userspace does the parsing; the kernel only validates against this
silicon (level 4.2 = 1920x1088, 4:2:0 8-bit, <=16 refs) and translates
into the firmware message format, which is intentionally not attempted
until R2 pins the mailbox ABI: apple_vxd_submit() refuses jobs with
-EAGAIN and states so once in the log.

NV12 is the only capture format for now; P010/NV16 follow the
HEVC/4:2:2 verification.  v4l2-compliance is expected to still fail on
request-API paths until submission is real.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
